From 9a35c308142ae28aef18cc53242f183a428f3115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: workspace-agent <workspace.vm.agent@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:20:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/56] m3 particles: PARC emitter copies emit from their own
 bones

PARC records were skipped (UnsupportedEntry), so an emitter with copies
emitted from its own bone only, and one whose own rate is 0 not at all.
Helios: one jet fire instead of four; no end smoke or end fire.

- parsers/m3/particlecopy.ts reads PARC (rate, partEmit, bone).
- ParticleEmitter reads copyIndices (offsets from m3addon per version).
- M3ParticleSystem: each copy is an emission slot of the emitter
  (WhiteoutFlakes): own bone, rate and carry, one particle pool. Births
  go to world space on the copy's bone, then back to emitter space for
  an emitter-space emitter. Sizes scale by the bone's scale over the
  emitter's (WhiteoutFlakes sizeBlend).
- slotSpawned counts births per slot, for the tests.

Known defects:
- partEmit bursts are not run, for emitters or copies.
- Copy semantics ported from WhiteoutFlakes; not compared with the game.
